&lt;p&gt;We’re one of the fastest‑growing private companies and a leading player in a massive, fast‑moving market. With a global workforce, we’re remote‑first and grounded in a simple idea: software is a people business. Cribl is the place where curious, collaborative people can do their best work, grow fast, and bring their full selves to the herd.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(224, 62, 45);&quot;&gt;Location: France&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Partner Solutions Engineer, Southern Europe, you’ll be the technical face of Cribl for our strategic partners across Southern Europe, enabling partner presales and consultants to run high-quality discoveries, PoVs, and deployments themselves. You will also have the opportunity to own and run pre-sales engagements within the commercial territory.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll own partner-facing enablement programs and ongoing technical communities. You’ll collaborate closely with Cribl sales, partner managers, and distributors to build repeatable patterns that our partners can take to market at scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will help partners and customers understand the value of Cribl during the sales process, provide demonstrations and be the technical authority throughout the engagement to ensure the business benefits Cribl provides are understood.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As An Active Member Of Our Team, You Will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and coach Partners value pillars, use cases and business cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide architecture expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of Cribl University tracks, NFR environments and online resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal confidence, velocity, and account activities by aligning Cribl and partner sales activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase partner co-sell contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain partner status and contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are a remote-first company and work happens across many time-zones - you may be required to occasionally perform duties outside your standard working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;If You’ve Got It - We Want It&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Channel Partners - experience of partner engagement, enablement and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+yrs in Sales Engineering, Professional Services, or Consulting, working with cloud and SaaS based technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Logs, Metrics, IT Operations, and/or Security, ideally in observability, SIEM, or data platform contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience designing and delivering technical enablement (trainings, bootcamps, workshops, or office hours) for partner or customer technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling and presales skills—you can translate complex data architectures into simple, value-driven narratives and coach others to do the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run high-impact discovery with technical and business stakeholders to understand current tooling, data flows, constraints, and success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with proof-of-value or proof-of-concept projects, including defining success criteria, evaluation plans, and clear executive summaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Cribl in the partner community via events, webinars, and user groups as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with multiple operating systems (proficiency with Linux is desired).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of JavaScript and Regex, or similar scripting and data-manipulation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 40% to customers, partners, and event locations as needed. Some international travel is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of MEDDPICC, Command of the Message or any solution selling methodology, advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud Platform certifications advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and English is required, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-Italian, Spanish and Portuguese language proficiency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are based in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-GV1&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary for this role is dependent on country of employment and will be based on the individual candidate&#39;s job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to base salary, for sales and some sales-adjacent roles, employees are eligible to earn incentive compensation (commission). For all other roles, employees are eligible to participate in the Cribl Corporate Bonus Program.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, Cribl offers a benefits package that may include retirement/pension support, paid holidays and paid time off, remote office setup support, equity, and other wellness and support programs. Benefits vary by country in accordance with local requirements and market practice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€97.400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€122.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring Your Whole Self&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Diversity drives innovation, enables better decisions to support our customers, and inspires change for the better. We’re building a culture where differences are valued and welcomed, and we work together to bring out the best in each other. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or any other applicable legally protected characteristics in the location in which the candidate is applying.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Interested in joining the Cribl herd? Learn more about the smartest, funniest, most passionate goats you’ll ever meet at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cribl.io/about-us/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;cribl.io/about-us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: &lt;/strong&gt;Senior Engineer I&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris (Hybrid)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; €54,000 - €70,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Client Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting To:&lt;/strong&gt; Software Engineering Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Paris and requires an existing right to work in France. At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today’s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform orchestrates millions of real-time decisions across homes, devices, markets and grids. By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable, affordable and adaptive to everyday life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Write clean, well-tested, and maintainable TypeScript to build and extend Kaluza’s platform for major clients including ENGIE, taking ownership of features from conception to deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud-Native Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Build, deploy, and maintain highly scalable applications on AWS Serverless (e.g., Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB) and help design event-driven microservices with real-time data streaming via Kafka.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Integration: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify and implement opportunities to embed AI into Kaluza’s platform and software development life-cycle - LLM-powered automation, intelligent decision support, and AI-assisted workflows. Act as an AI knowledge carrier, sharing learnings across teams and helping build a culture of AI-informed engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Quality &amp;amp; Mentorship: &lt;/strong&gt;Champion engineering best practices through thorough code reviews and upskilling junior engineers on TypeScript, serverless, and AI development patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: Collaborate closely with your team, Product Managers, and Engineering Managers to refine features, estimate tasks, and deliver value predictably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally you&#39;ll have/be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TypeScript Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong professional experience building scalable, production-grade applications using TypeScript and Node.js, including on AWS Serverless architectures (Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB) and event-driven systems such as Kafka.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;You think about AI as a practical engineering tool — curious about what’s possible, focused on what’s production-ready, and motivated to bring colleagues along with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;A track record of creative problem-solving and delivering team-level technical expertise on complex application workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile Practices: &lt;/strong&gt;A solid grasp of CI/CD pipelines, software development fundamentals, and Agile/Lean methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communicator: &lt;/strong&gt;Excellent communication skills and a genuine enjoyment of cross-functional teamwork, including explaining technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will set you apart:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LLM Integration Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Hands-on experience integrating large language models into production applications, whether via APIs (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, AWS Bedrock) or open-source models, with a solid understanding of prompt engineering, context management, and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tooling Advocacy: &lt;/strong&gt;A track record of introducing AI-assisted developer tooling and workflows (e.g., Copilot, Cursor, Claude or similar) into a team and upskilling colleagues, not just using it personally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Energy or Enterprise Domain Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Background working with large enterprise applications, specifically involving billing, ledger tooling, payments integration, or energy grid/supply data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client-Facing Awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; Previous experience working on consulting, software-as-a-service (SaaS) onboarding, or client-delivery technical projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you&#39;re excited about joining us and think you have some of what we&#39;re looking for, even if you&#39;re not 100% sure, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about working in Kaluza on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can also find our Applicant Data Protection Policy&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/applicant-data-protection-notice/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job title:&lt;/strong&gt; Product Manager (Billing)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris — Hybrid (3 days in office)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; €57,600 - €72,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Product Management - Billing &amp;amp; Payments&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to: &lt;/strong&gt;Head of Product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in Paris, France and requires the successful candidate to be based in or willing to relocate to Paris. Fluent French and English (spoken and written) are essential for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please submit your profile in English.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today&#39;s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future. Leveraging Data, AI, and real-time decision-making we turn energy complexity into growth opportunities for our partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable and affordable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the localisation efforts for our global energy billing platform, ensuring it meets the specific regulatory, market, and cultural requirements of France, from meter read to bill.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll be in charge of the French localisation of the Billing Module—one of the core product domains at the heart of the Kaluza platform. The Billing module processes consumption, pricing, and account data to schedule, calculate, and generate accurate, timely, and compliant invoices throughout a customer’s lifecycle. The module automatically manages billing cycles, generates bills, handles corrections, and produces the data that feeds invoices, billing-related communications, payment schedules, and downstream financial reporting, while powering customer and agent UIs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, full-stack product role — you&#39;ll work across the whole domain and alongside PMs from other domains and from the global billing teams to ensure the overall billing&amp;nbsp; journey from meter to bill meets the requirements of French clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate intensely with clients and in-country experts&lt;/strong&gt; to understand their unique needs and requirements, negotiate scope, and build a roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep dive into French energy market regulations&lt;/strong&gt;, translating complex compliance needs into detailed product specifications for the billing system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and manage detailed product requirements &lt;/strong&gt;for features related to country-specific needs from getting a read to generating a bill (meter reading protocols, invoice formats, taxation rules, payment methods, and regulatory reporting).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work closely with engineering, UX, and QA teams &lt;/strong&gt;to ensure the successful implementation and testing of localised billing functionalities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as the go-to expert &lt;/strong&gt;for global teams on specific French market nuances related to energy billing and customer journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuously monitor changes in French energy legislation&lt;/strong&gt; and market practices, proactively adapting the product roadmap to maintain compliance and competitiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally you&#39;ll have/be:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven experience as a Product Manager, or equivalent role in software companies&lt;/strong&gt;, with a strong track record of successfully localising complex software products for international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solid understanding of the end-to-end B2C billing lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt; including meter data, tariffs, invoicing, and debt management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record in regulated markets where billing complexity matters, &lt;/strong&gt;energy, telecoms, financial services, or similar. Familiarity with the French energy market (ENGIE, CRE, switching, tariff structures) is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional ability to translate abstract regulatory text or client requirements into clear, actionable, outcome-driven requirements for development teams.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience collaborating with cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; (engineering, design, legal, operations, client success) to deliver localised solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent stakeholder and client management skills&lt;/strong&gt;, able to lead conversations across requirements, scope, expectations, and roadmap alignment, and communicate technical &amp;amp; market complexity clearly to varied audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proficiency in AI tools throughout all stages of the product lifecycle — from discovery and ideation to delivery and iteration.Fluent in French and English&lt;/strong&gt; — our platform and many of our teams operate in English, so you move easily between both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A builder&#39;s mindset&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;re autonomous, learn fast, and aren&#39;t afraid to go deep. You&#39;re comfortable interrogating a codebase with AI tools, reading an API schema or data model, and writing a SQL query to get the answer you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and pace&lt;/strong&gt; — you can operate effectively when not everything is defined, know when to make a call, and aren&#39;t afraid to escalate or ask for help when it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and very comfortable in English&lt;/strong&gt; — our platform and many of our teams operate in English, so you move easily between both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
